---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.njk",
  title: "Collectibles",
  seoTitle: "GTA 6 Collectibles: Every Set, How Many and What 100% Needs",
  description: "Every GTA 6 collectible set: 480 cards in 18 sets, 125 Cocaine Flamingos, 18 meditation spots, WAiNK scans and more, with what 100% needs and a counter that saves your progress.",
  eleventyComputed: {
    sample: (data) => !!data.db.collectibles.sample,
    updated: (data) => data.db.collectibles.updated,
  },
}
---
{%- set c = db.collectibles %}
<header class="mast" style="--glow:var(--cyan)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Collectibles and 100%</p>
    <h1>Hidden Leonida</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Every collectible set in GTA 6, how many there are, what the 100% checklist wants and how to find them. Count as you go; the numbers are shared with the map tracker.</p>
    {%- if c.types.length %}
    <div class="progress" data-ctr-total>
      <div class="row"><span class="lab">Toward 100%</span><span class="pct"><span data-ctr-done>0</span> / <span data-ctr-max>0</span> · <span data-ctr-pct>0%</span></span></div>
      <div class="bar"><i></i></div>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</header>

{%- if not c.types.length %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="empty">
      <p class="kicker">Being filled in</p>
      <h2 class="sec-h sm">Collectibles get mapped as we find them</h2>
      <p>Each set gets its own page here, with locations grouped by region and a checklist, once we have confirmed it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- else %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="sec-h">The sets</h2>
    <p class="lede">{{ c.types.length }} collectible sets count toward 100%. Open one for how it works and what counts. Location lists are added once we have confirmed them.</p>
    <div class="ctypes">
      {%- for t in c.types %}
      <article class="ctype">
        <h3><a href="/collectibles/{{ t.slug }}/">{{ t.name }}</a></h3>
        <p class="desc">{{ t.desc }}</p>
        <dl class="cfacts">
          {%- if t.total %}<div><dt>In the game</dt><dd>{{ t.total }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
          {%- if t.need %}<div><dt>100% needs</dt><dd>{{ t.need }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        </dl>
        {%- if t.ctr %}{% set ctr = t.ctr %}{% set label = t.counterLabel %}{% include "partials/ctr.njk" %}{% endif %}
        <a class="more" href="/collectibles/{{ t.slug }}/">How to find them →</a>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec-tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="lede">More to count: stunts, races, robberies and the rest of the 100% list are on the <a href="/map/#tracker">map tracker</a> and the <a href="/guides/100-percent-checklist/">100% checklist</a>. For activities and cheats, see <a href="/guides/activities-and-collectibles/">activities and collectibles</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if c.mapped %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="sec-h">Where to look</h2>
    <p class="lede">Which sets turn up in which region, for clearing the map one area at a time.</p>
    <div class="regions">
      {%- for r in regions %}
      <div class="region">
        <span class="pin">◉ {{ r.kind }}</span>
        <h3><a href="/map/{{ r.slug }}/">{{ r.short or r.name }}</a></h3>
        <div class="here">
          {%- for t in c.types %}{% if r.slug in t.regions %}<a href="/collectibles/{{ t.slug }}/">{{ t.name }}</a>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
